/// Retail sales and profit: the simplest model in this repository, and
/// deliberately so.
///
/// The other models here are clinical and manufacturing ones, and a reviewer
/// made the same point about them four times in one session: "if you are not
/// able to understand these things, you will not be able to correlate, because
/// you don't know what is Clinical Trial Safety... you can make a simple one,
/// like use profit and sales information". Somebody evaluating a documentation
/// tool should be spending their attention on the documentation, not on
/// learning what a protocol deviation is.
///
/// So this model is built from figures everyone already knows -- units, price,
/// cost, sales, profit, margin -- and its measures are the ones on the first
/// row of every retail dashboard ever built. Total Sales really is unit price
/// times units sold, exactly as she described it.
model Model
	culture: en-GB
	defaultPowerBIDataSourceVersion: powerBI_V3

ref table Sales
ref table Product
ref table Customer
ref table Store
ref table Calendar
ref table 'Sales Metrics'
